  The block preamble (lines 815-829) explicitly documents the
  short-circuit contract this writer's no-op contract depends on:

    # Setting{Charge,Distance,Temperature,TirePressure}Unit
    # (setting_unit, IsSettingUnit=true). normalize.observeSettingUnit
    # short-circuits the toSI + router.Route path for these four
    # atomics: Pipeline.processOne checks meta.IsSettingUnit first and
    # writes to vehicle_unit_history via unithistory.Repo.Record so
    # subsequent unit-bearing values look up the correct active unit at
    # write time. The router is NOT consulted for these fields at
    # runtime (processOne returns before reaching router.Route).

Check 2: normalize.Pipeline.processOne short-circuit (lines 191-212)
  command: view internal/tesla/normalize/pipeline.go view_range=[191,212]
  result: (verbatim)
    func (p *Pipeline) processOne(ctx context.Context, atomic codec.Atomic, vehicleIntID int64) {
      meta := protomodel.SignalsByName[atomic.Field]

      // Setting*Unit atomics short-circuit the toSI + router.Route
      // path. They land in vehicle_unit_history and stop there; per
      // ADR-004 #8 the SettingDistanceUnit / SettingTemperatureUnit /
      // SettingTirePressureUnit / SettingChargeUnit Fields are not
      // routed to any hot table.
      if meta != nil && meta.IsSettingUnit {
        if err := p.observeSettingUnit(ctx, atomic, vehicleIntID); err != nil {
          p.metrics.ValuesProcessed.WithLabelValues(atomic.Field, outcomeError).Inc()
          p.log.Warn().
            Err(err).
            Str("field", atomic.Field).
            Int64("vehicle_id", vehicleIntID).
            Time("emitted_at", atomic.EmittedAt).
            Msg("normalize: setting-unit observer failed")
          return
        }
        p.metrics.ValuesProcessed.WithLabelValues(atomic.Field, outcomeOK).Inc()
        return
      }

  This is the production path that ensures the no-op writer's Write
  method is unreachable in steady state. The two `return` statements
  inside the IsSettingUnit branch are the structural guarantees.

